- Reduced motion does not animate. `npm run lint` is clean.

## QA follow-ups

The prototype in `docs/design/mesh-view.html` is the layout source. These corrections land in this task:

- Containment is one bus: a stem under the focus, a horizontal run across the columns, then a spine and short stub to each record. The shared leaf column has no head.
- The focus and its parent sit on the center of the columns.
- “Linked to this” is a labeled row to the right of the focus, level with the parent. “Linked from inside” labels the right rail, which starts to the right of both the columns and that top row.
- Titles wrap to two lines, the reference sits on the next line, and the focused record is larger. A record from another project shows that project’s number (`N0057 · P0009`) when the app already has it.
- The canvas is a dotted plotting table. Reference lines are dashed so they stay distinct from the bus.
- Breadcrumbs are titles separated by ›. When the focus belongs to another project, the toolbar adds “Back to {this project}”. Visit Back stays for one step inside the project.
- Pan stays at a readable size. The prototype’s fit-to-width shrinks a project as wide as TaskMesh.
